# Casting Sanar's prepare spell unprepares it as it is cast (CR 722.3d), so a Wild Idea that is countered still leaves Sanar unprepared
# and nothing is found: Bot2 answers with Counterspell (two Mox Sapphires). The copy of the card ceases to exist (a copy of a card in
# the graveyard is not a card, CR 707.10a, 704.5e). Casting it still counts as casting a sorcery spell, so Sanar can make its Treasure.
# Bot1's library holds a Lightning Bolt, which a resolved Wild Idea would have fetched: it stays in the library, the hand holds only Plains.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Sanar, Unfinished Genius
Plains
Plains
Lightning Bolt
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire x2
Counterspell
Plains x17

